From a6fb6d8823a6f893807a08fa6908c9fa256b8b85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:42:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(activation): global-plugin front door + lazy .forge home
 (PR1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Activation foundation (epic 64d6c458): one coherent front-door story
reconciling C1's global plugin, C4's `activation` bootstrap skill, and the
epic's auto-init. Portable by construction — works in a BARE repo with no
.forge/ and no forge-workflow dependency.

- plugin/: minimal Claude Code plugin scaffold (.claude-plugin/plugin.json)
  matching the real superpowers/beads format; carries ONLY the new
  `activation` skill (does NOT repackage the 93-project-ref canonical skills)
  + a read-only SessionStart nudge via the superpowers run-hook.cmd Windows
  wrapper. Self-marketplace at .claude-plugin/marketplace.json (source ./plugin).
- skills/activation: orient-first bootstrap — detects project type, STATES
  findings, offers bare-minimum setup without forcing, declares next step (/plan).
- lib/activation/ensure-forge-home.js: lazy ensureForgeHome() wired at the
  executeCommand choke point. First MUTATING verb creates ONLY a gates-disabled
  .forge/config.yaml (minimal adoption profile); read-only verbs write nothing;
  existing .forge/ is never clobbered. No hooks/lefthook/protected-paths/.mcp.

Tests: 25 unit+integration (test/activation/) + real-CLI bare-repo smoke.
Refs 64d6c458.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
